# LOG .gitignore
#
# LOG is a personal ROM hack. The repository carries the code that BUILDS the hack, never the game data it
# builds from or produces. Nothing here is a copyright notice: it is the list of what must never be pushed.
#
# CLAUDE.md names builds\, data\ and zhack\. The real rule is wider, so this file is the rule:
# archive\ and scratch\ hold 446 ROM, save and state files between them, 3.3 GB and 1.3 GB.

# ===== folders that hold game data =====
# data\      the owner's own ROM dumps, rips and references. Never redistributable, and never written to.
# builds\    every build ROM, with its .sav and savestates.
# zhack\     another modder's hack: the source ROM, its IPS patch, and the study sheets taken from it.
# archive\   dated copies of old builds, art rounds and snapshots. 3.3 GB, and full of ROMs.
# scratch\   throwaway: test ROMs, sprite exports, ROM copies, the Python environment, Ghidra projects. 1.3 GB.
builds/
data/
zhack/
archive/
scratch/
scripts/permanent/map-editor/assets/

# ===== game data by extension, anywhere =====
# Belt and braces. A ROM, a save or a savestate that lands outside the folders above is still barred.
# The Z Hack ROM proved the need: it sat in docs\, where no folder rule reached it.
*.gba
*.gb
*.gbc
*.sav
*.srm
*.ss[0-9]
*.ips
*.bps
*.ups

# BizHawk writes these two names during a capture run (scripts\permanent\emu\capture.py).
*.SaveRAM
*.State

# ===== generated output =====
# scripts\one-time\  one dated folder per study: 205 MB of probe listings, ROM copies and a Ghidra log.
#                    The study reports in docs\tasks\ carry the findings, which is what a reader needs.
# test-data\         the save files the tests read. They are game data.
scripts/one-time/
test-data/

# ===== Python and editor =====
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
LOG.code-workspace

# ===== art: finished work only =====
# The zhack\ layout is the model: a finalized sprite list, not a working folder. Scratch art, working rounds,
# mockup frames, review GIFs and ripped vanilla sheets never go up (owner, 2026-10-31).
#
# Three things are kept, and nothing else:
#   1. build inputs      the patch modules read these, so a clone cannot build the ROM without them
#   2. finished art      the finalized portraits and the master swatch
#   3. art\tables\       palette.json and portraits.json, read by art_inject
#
# Gohan's gi sets are NOT finished art. They are here only because gohan_gi is line 1 of the main build
# list. Remove the four gi lines below to drop them, and a clean clone then cannot build r40.
art/*

# The tree below is the 2026-11-13 layout. Each rule names a folder that now exists; the old flat
# names (gi_base, portrait-sources, vanilla-sets) are gone, so a rule naming one would silently
# untrack his art. That is exactly what happened mid-move and is why these are grouped by subject.

# --- build inputs and his own drawings, by subject ---
!art/tables/
!art/ui/
!art/maps/
!art/effects/
!art/palettes/
!art/hand-fixes/
!art/locks/

# characters: the gi sets the dev master reads, his tank art, and the Cell aura the build reads.
!art/characters/
art/characters/*
!art/characters/gohan/
art/characters/gohan/*
!art/characters/gohan/gi_base/
!art/characters/gohan/gi_ssj_v2/
!art/characters/gohan/gi_ssj2_aura/
!art/characters/gohan/gi_rage_aura/
!art/characters/gohan/golden/
!art/characters/trunks/
!art/characters/cell/
art/characters/cell/*
!art/characters/cell/aura/
art/characters/cell/aura/*
!art/characters/cell/aura/scale_15/

# portraits: the finished ones, his sources and the kit. The vanilla export is a ROM rip, kept out.
!art/portraits/
art/portraits/vanilla/

# reference: base-audit's approved frames only. vanilla-sets, anim and sheets are rips and review.
!art/reference/
art/reference/*
!art/reference/base-audit/
art/reference/base-audit/*
!art/reference/base-audit/approved/
!art/reference/base-audit/gi_master_swatch.png
# gohan_portraits READS this sheet, so a clone cannot build the masters without it.
!art/reference/sheets/
art/reference/sheets/*
!art/reference/sheets/portraits_review.png

# --- the eight power-up frames he drew, and nothing else from the kits ---
!art/kits/
art/kits/*
!art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/
art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/*
!art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/Frame_1.png
!art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/Frame_2.png
!art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/his-edit/
art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/his-edit/*
!art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/his-edit/v2/
art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/his-edit/v2/*
!art/kits/2026-11-12-vegeta-powerup/his-edit/v2/build-ready/
!art/kits/2026-11-12-piccolo-powerup/
art/kits/2026-11-12-piccolo-powerup/*
!art/kits/2026-11-12-piccolo-powerup/P_Frame1.png
!art/kits/2026-11-12-piccolo-powerup/P_Frame2.png
!art/kits/2026-11-12-piccolo-powerup/P_Frame3.png
!art/kits/2026-11-12-piccolo-powerup/P_Frame4.png

# --- the owner build folder stays out ---
# It is his live working folder. Nothing here reads it, writes to it or deletes from it, and
# tracking it would mean reading it. He decides whether it goes up.

# ===== local working files, not part of the hack =====
# CLAUDE.md drives the local tooling. It is not something a modder cloning this needs, and the repository
# should not carry assistant-specific files. It stays on disk and out of the repository.
CLAUDE.md

# Another modder's hack, kept for clean-room study only. Never published, never copied into our art.
kai/

# The ledger is my day-by-day work diary, not something a modder cloning this needs.
# It stays on disk and keeps being written; it just does not go to the repository.
docs/ledger/

# The superpowers skill workspace: per-plan ledgers, briefs and review packages. Session scratch.
.superpowers/

# The map editor's crash-recovery snapshots. One file per autosave tick, 30 of them for one map.
# The owner's real work is in map-editor\maps\ and map-editor\library\, which ARE kept.
scripts/permanent/map-editor/autosave/
# The editor's other two recovery folders, for the same reason as autosave\: maps\older\ holds one
# timestamped snapshot per save (24 of them for map 142), and library\deleted\ is its recycle bin.
# Git history is the durable record of both, and these two folders grow without a bound.
scripts/permanent/map-editor/maps/older/
scripts/permanent/map-editor/library/deleted/

# Pre-merge copies of the whole bible, written by merge_bible_rows.py before 2026-11-13.
# Each is a full 1.1 MB copy of docs\RE-BIBLE.md. A task folder holds inputs, never outputs,
# and git history is the durable record of what the bible said before a merge.
RE-BIBLE.before-merge.md
